## Summary

Fixes the stile issue a-thoren found while testing #366: "you can jump over the stile from too far away and the code assumes you're right next to it, meaning you don't always end up in the sheep pen". The cause is the shared `StileScript` (every `fullstyle` stile, including the Sheep Shearer pen's), so this is its own change rather than part of #366.

`StileScript.climbStile` climbed from the player's tile wherever the interaction ended, e.g. a tile diagonal to the stile or beside it along the fence, so the forced move could start and end on the wrong tiles. It now takes the stile's footprint tile on the player's side of the fence, walks the player onto it (`playerMove`), and then climbs to the other footprint tile, the same way the Port Sarim stile on `main` does. If the player can't reach the start tile, nothing happens.

